{
  "id": "live-visualization",
  "content": {
    "description": [
      [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A speculative visualization of the individual’s influence on the flow of time, as outlined in the spiral treatise. An afterimage of the viewer modulates between the present and a user-defined delay into the past; delay and modulation speed are adjustable on the controller. The work offers a sense of agency over time while asking how much control we truly have."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "The controller case was modeled in Rhino 8 with Grasshopper and PLA 3D printed in white filament; a clear acrylic layer protects the laser-cut clock hands. The live visualization runs in Max 9 with Arduino code."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    ],
